<div>
	<h1 class='text-3xl font-bold mb-8'>About Marie Skłodowska Curie</h1>
	<p class='mb-6 text-lg'>
		Marie Skłodowska Curie (1867–1934) was a Polish-born physicist and chemist whose experimental research helped establish the study of radioactivity. Working with Pierre Curie, she identified polonium and radium in 1898 and later isolated radium for further study.
	</p>
	<p class='mb-6 text-lg'>
		She received the 1903 Nobel Prize in Physics with Pierre Curie and Henri Becquerel, then the 1911 Nobel Prize in Chemistry. This demonstration presents a small selection of her publications, a brief academic timeline, and modern historical notes about her research.
	</p>
</div>
